1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,666
Therefore we still have witches and wizards amongst us.

2
00:00:04,966 --> 00:00:08,499
He is more powerful than all the rest of us together.

3
00:00:08,799 --> 00:00:11,865
I am anxious to get back to my aunt and uncle,

4
00:00:12,165 --> 00:00:14,031
Can you help me find my way?

5
00:00:14,331 --> 00:00:18,131
there is a great desert, and none could live to cross it.

6
00:00:18,431 --> 00:00:21,164
Then you must go to the City of Emeralds.

7
00:00:21,464 --> 00:00:23,130
Perhaps Oz will help you.

8
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:24,696
Where is this city?

9
00:00:24,996 --> 00:00:27,062
the Great Wizard I told you of.

10
00:00:27,362 --> 00:00:28,562
Is he a good man?

11
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:33,595
However, I will use all the magic arts I know of to keep you from harm.

12
00:00:33,895 --> 00:00:39,428
and no one will dare injure a person who has been kissed by the Witch of the North.

13
00:00:39,728 --> 00:00:45,128
They would be just the thing to take a long walk in, for they could not wear out.

14
00:00:45,428 --> 00:00:50,961
Besides, you have white in your frock, and only witches and sorceresses wear white.

15
00:00:51,261 --> 00:00:56,661
It is better for people to keep away from Oz, unless they have business with him.

16
00:00:56,961 --> 00:00:58,161
Did you speak?

17
00:00:58,461 --> 00:00:59,727
Can’t you get down?

18
00:01:00,027 --> 00:01:01,493
I feel like a new man.

19
00:01:01,793 --> 00:01:03,126
Why, don’t you know?

20
00:01:03,426 --> 00:01:05,026
He can’t hurt the straw.

21
00:01:05,326 --> 00:01:06,726
it’s a lighted match.

22
00:01:07,026 --> 00:01:08,892
There is no place like home.

23
00:01:09,192 --> 00:01:13,058
It is such an uncomfortable feeling to know one is a fool.

24
00:01:13,358 --> 00:01:14,558
Shall we go there?

25
00:01:14,858 --> 00:01:16,124
I am all tired out.

26
00:01:16,424 --> 00:01:20,157
They are rusted so badly that I cannot move them at all;

27
00:01:20,457 --> 00:01:22,857
Why didn’t you walk around the hole?

28
00:01:23,157 --> 00:01:25,823
My head is stuffed with straw, you know,

29
00:01:26,123 --> 00:01:29,389
I will tell you my story, and then you will know.

30
00:01:29,689 --> 00:01:34,689
When they scratched against the tin it made a cold shiver run down my back.

31
00:01:34,989 --> 00:01:39,055
For my part, I have no heart; so I cannot have heart disease.

32
00:01:39,355 --> 00:01:42,888
for you will help to keep away the other wild beasts.

33
00:01:43,188 --> 00:01:45,588
but that doesn’t make me any braver,

34
00:01:45,888 --> 00:01:49,754
for you can carry us all over on your back, one at a time.

35
00:01:50,054 --> 00:01:53,454
or the Tin Woodman badly dented on the rocks below.

36
00:01:53,754 --> 00:01:55,554
Why don’t you run and jump?

37
00:01:55,854 --> 00:01:57,720
but the kind Stork saved me,

38
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:00,686
I always like to help anyone in trouble.

39
00:02:00,986 --> 00:02:04,786
and get out of this deadly flower bed as soon as you can.

40
00:02:05,086 --> 00:02:07,619
We will bring the little girl with us,

41
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:09,119
Oh, thank you!

42
00:02:09,419 --> 00:02:12,685
Oh, your Majesty, we thought you would be killed!

43
00:02:12,985 --> 00:02:18,585
Oh, yes; you can save our friend, the Cowardly Lion, who is asleep in the poppy bed.

44
00:02:18,885 --> 00:02:21,285
But, comrades, what shall we do now?

45
00:02:21,585 --> 00:02:24,518
and then we can keep on to the Emerald City.

46
00:02:24,818 --> 00:02:29,151
Why, it is said that he never lets anyone come into his presence.

47
00:02:29,451 --> 00:02:32,917
nor do I know of any living person who has seen him.

48
00:02:33,217 --> 00:02:35,417
and some say he looks like a cat.

49
00:02:35,717 --> 00:02:38,850
And we have been told that Oz is a good Wizard.

50
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:43,683
But to those who are not honest, or who approach him from curiosity,

51
00:02:43,983 --> 00:02:46,849
and if you wish for anything ring the bell.

52
00:02:47,149 --> 00:02:49,682
Oz will send for you tomorrow morning.

53
00:02:49,982 --> 00:02:51,182
if he will see me.

54
00:02:51,482 --> 00:02:54,015
Then he asked me what you looked like,

55
00:02:54,315 --> 00:02:57,648
and he decided he would admit you to his presence.

56
00:02:57,948 --> 00:03:00,281
Where did you get the silver shoes?

57
00:03:00,581 --> 00:03:01,781
But I cannot!

58
00:03:02,081 --> 00:03:05,747
Even if I wanted to, how could I kill the Wicked Witch?

59
00:03:06,047 --> 00:03:08,847
I am only a Scarecrow, stuffed with straw.

60
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:10,547
Why should I do this?

61
00:03:10,847 --> 00:03:13,713
I am a Cowardly Lion, afraid of everything.

62
00:03:14,013 --> 00:03:18,479
so that in reality I may become the King of Beasts, as men call me.

63
00:03:18,779 --> 00:03:23,445
I suppose we must try it; but I am sure I do not want to kill anybody,

64
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:26,011
No one ever wishes to go that way.

65
00:03:26,311 --> 00:03:29,711
so get behind me and I will meet them as they come.

66
00:03:30,011 --> 00:03:32,077
and the bees cannot sting them.

67
00:03:32,377 --> 00:03:35,510
You have called us for the third and last time.

68
00:03:35,810 --> 00:03:38,676
and that is greater than the Power of Evil.

69
00:03:38,976 --> 00:03:43,909
I can still make her my slave, for she does not know how to use her power.

70
00:03:44,209 --> 00:03:45,409
I can starve you.

71
00:03:45,709 --> 00:03:47,442
You are a wicked creature!

72
00:03:47,742 --> 00:03:50,542
You have no right to take my shoe from me.

73
00:03:50,842 --> 00:03:52,375
See what you have done!

74
00:03:52,675 --> 00:03:55,675
Well, in a few minutes I shall be all melted,

75
00:03:55,975 --> 00:03:57,908
I have been wicked in my day,

76
00:03:58,208 --> 00:04:00,408
Are any of your people tinsmiths?

77
00:04:00,708 --> 00:04:05,974
and bend him back into shape again, and solder him together where he is broken?

78
00:04:06,274 --> 00:04:10,474
I’ll chop it down, and then we can get the Scarecrow’s clothes.

79
00:04:10,774 --> 00:04:12,707
at last I shall get my heart.

80
00:04:13,007 --> 00:04:16,473
It seems to me I can scarcely wait till I get to Oz,

81
00:04:16,773 --> 00:04:19,906
and you must admit this is a very long journey.

82
00:04:20,206 --> 00:04:22,539
Why didn’t we think of that before?

83
00:04:22,839 --> 00:04:24,705
Now the Golden Cap is yours,

84
00:04:25,005 --> 00:04:26,271
Why do you seek me?

85
00:04:26,571 --> 00:04:30,904
Well, come to me tomorrow, for I must have time to think it over.

86
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:35,804
But don’t strike me—please don’t—and I’ll do anything you want me to.

87
00:04:36,104 --> 00:04:37,304
Exactly so!

88
00:04:37,604 --> 00:04:41,004
How was it that you appeared to me as a great Head?

89
00:04:41,304 --> 00:04:44,570
I ordered them to build this City, and my Palace;

90
00:04:44,870 --> 00:04:50,403
I’m not much of a magician, as I said; but if you will come to me tomorrow morning,

91
00:04:50,703 --> 00:04:56,036
I cannot tell you how to use them, however; you must find that out for yourself.

92
00:04:56,336 --> 00:04:58,402
how am I to get back to Kansas?

93
00:04:58,702 --> 00:05:04,102
Hereafter you will be a great man, for I have given you a lot of bran-new brains.

94
00:05:04,402 --> 00:05:06,068
I have come for my heart.

95
00:05:06,368 --> 00:05:11,634
Sit down, my dear; I think I have found the way to get you out of this country.

96
00:05:11,934 --> 00:05:13,200
And back to Kansas?

97
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:18,966
I have plenty of silk in the Palace, so it will be no trouble to make the balloon.

98
00:05:19,266 --> 00:05:21,666
I am now going away to make a visit.

99
00:05:21,966 --> 00:05:23,632
Oz was always our friend.

100
00:05:23,932 --> 00:05:27,198
I should like to cry a little because Oz is gone,
